{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fc7ghtK2tDLyFexYNo5HUh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd039-env\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/env: Run a Command in a Modified Environment\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Shell scripts and build systems frequently need to run commands with a controlled set of\n6\t  environment variables, adding, removing, or replacing entries before exec. The macOS BSD\n7\t  env lacks GNU extensions such as -C (chdir) and -S (split string), but the core flags\n8\t  (-i, -u, NAME=VALUE) are shared. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU\n9\t  reference binary (genv, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all supported flag\n10\t  combinations and edge cases, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n11\t\n12\tgoals:\n13\t  - G1: Print the current environment when invoked with no arguments and no COMMAND.\n14\t  - G2: Run COMMAND in a modified environment, inheriting, unsetting, or overriding variables as directed by flags and NAME=VALUE pairs.\n15\t  - G3: Support starting from an empty environment (-i) to give full control over what COMMAND inherits.\n16\t  - G4: Support NUL-delimited output (-0) for safe parsing of values that contain newlines.\n17\t\n18\trequirements:\n19\t  R1:\n20\t    title: Default behavior\n21\t    items:\n22\t      - R1.1:\n23\t          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print every environment variable on its own line in NAME=VALUE format and exit 0.\n24\t      - R1.2:\n25\t          text: When invoked with COMMAND [ARG ...], must execute COMMAND with the resulting environment after all modifications have been applied.\n26\t      - R1.3:\n27\t          text: If COMMAND is not found, must exit 127. If COMMAND is found but cannot be executed, must exit 126.\n28\t\n29\t  R2:\n30\t    title: Environment modification\n31\t    items:\n32\t      - R2.1:\n33\t          text: -i or --ignore-environment must start COMMAND with an empty environment. Only explicitly supplied NAME=VALUE pairs appear in the child process environment.\n34\t      - R2.2:\n35\t          text: -u NAME or --unset=NAME must remove the variable NAME from the environment before COMMAND runs. Multiple -u flags must be supported.\n36\t      - R2.3:\n37\t          text: Each NAME=VALUE argument (positional, before COMMAND) must set or override the variable NAME in the environment. The first argument that does not contain '=' and is not a flag is the start of COMMAND.\n38\t\n39\t  R3:\n40\t    title: Output formatting and exit codes\n41\t    items:\n42\t      - R3.1:\n43\t          text: -0 or --null must terminate each output line with a NUL byte (0x00) instead of a newline when printing the environment (no COMMAND case).\n44\t      - R3.2:\n45\t          text: When COMMAND is executed, env must exit with the same exit code as COMMAND.\n46\t      - R3.3:\n47\t          text: Must print an error message to stderr when an invalid option is given and exit 125.\n48\t\n49\t  R4:\n50\t    title: Differential testing\n51\t    items:\n52\t      - R4.1:\n53\t          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (genv) via pkg/testutils.\n54\t      - R4.2:\n55\t          text: \"Tests must cover: no-argument environment dump, NAME=VALUE setting, -u unsetting, -i empty environment, -0 NUL-delimited output, COMMAND execution with modified env, and exit code passthrough.\"\n56\t      - R4.3:\n57\t          text: Tests must verify error output and exit code for invalid options and missing commands.\n58\t\n59\tnon_goals:\n60\t  - cmd/env does not implement -C (change directory) or -S (split string) GNU extensions.\n61\t  - cmd/env does not read variable assignments from stdin; all input comes from command-line arguments.\n62\t  - cmd/env does not perform shell expansion on COMMAND or its arguments; exec is direct.\n63\t\n64\tacceptance_criteria:\n65\t  - id: AC1\n66\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/env with no arguments produces the same output as genv with no arguments.\"\n67\t    traces:\n68\t      - R1.1\n69\t      - R1.2\n70\t      - R1.3\n71\t  - id: AC2\n72\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/env FOO=bar env prints an environment that includes FOO=bar, matching genv.\"\n73\t    traces:\n74\t      - R1.1\n75\t      - R1.2\n76\t      - R1.3\n77\t  - id: AC3\n78\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/env -i FOO=bar env produces only FOO=bar (plus any exec-injected variables), matching genv -i.\"\n79\t    traces:\n80\t      - R2.1\n81\t      - R4.2\n82\t  - id: AC4\n83\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/env -u HOME env omits HOME from the output, matching genv -u HOME.\"\n84\t    traces:\n85\t      - R2.2\n86\t      - R4.2\n87\t  - id: AC5\n88\t    criterion: \"Differential test against genv passes for environment dump, -i, -u, NAME=VALUE, -0, COMMAND execution, and exit code passthrough.\"\n89\t    traces:\n90\t      - R1.1\n91\t      - R1.3\n92\t      - R2.1\n93\t      - R2.2\n94\t      - R3.2\n95\t      - R3.3\n96\t      - R4.1\n97\t      - R4.2\n98\t      - R4.3\n99\t  - id: AC6\n100\t    criterion: \"cmd/env compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n101\t    traces:\n102\t      - R1.1\n103\t      - R1.2\n104\t      - R1.3\n105\t      - R2.1\n106\t      - R2.2\n107\t      - R2.3\n108\t      - R3.1\n109\t      - R3.2\n110\t      - R3.3\n111\t      - R4.1\n112\t      - R4.2\n113\t      - R4.3\n114\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d461bfc8-ec86-4b76-a705-0ddc369f10bf","uuid":"2b09bc3b-ce27-404c-9876-e1c812832225","timestamp":"2026-05-20T13:54:08.062Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5360/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd039-env.yaml","content":"id: srd039-env\ntitle: \"cmd/env: Run a Command in a Modified Environment\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Shell scripts and build systems frequently need to run commands with a controlled set of\n  environment variables, adding, removing, or replacing entries before exec. The macOS BSD\n  env lacks GNU extensions such as -C (chdir) and -S (split string), but the core flags\n  (-i, -u, NAME=VALUE) are shared. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU\n  reference binary (genv, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all supported flag\n  combinations and edge cases, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Print the current environment when invoked with no arguments and no COMMAND.\n  - G2: Run COMMAND in a modified environment, inheriting, unsetting, or overriding variables as directed by flags and NAME=VALUE pairs.\n  - G3: Support starting from an empty environment (-i) to give full control over what COMMAND inherits.\n  - G4: Support NUL-delimited output (-0) for safe parsing of values that contain newlines.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default behavior\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print every environment variable on its own line in NAME=VALUE format and exit 0.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: When invoked with COMMAND [ARG ...], must execute COMMAND with the resulting environment after all modifications have been applied.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: If COMMAND is not found, must exit 127. If COMMAND is found but cannot be executed, must exit 126.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Environment modification\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: -i or --ignore-environment must start COMMAND with an empty environment. Only explicitly supplied NAME=VALUE pairs appear in the child process environment.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: -u NAME or --unset=NAME must remove the variable NAME from the environment before COMMAND runs. Multiple -u flags must be supported.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Each NAME=VALUE argument (positional, before COMMAND) must set or override the variable NAME in the environment. The first argument that does not contain '=' and is not a flag is the start of COMMAND.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Output formatting and exit codes\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: -0 or --null must terminate each output line with a NUL byte (0x00) instead of a newline when printing the environment (no COMMAND case).\n      - R3.2:\n          text: When COMMAND is executed, env must exit with the same exit code as COMMAND.\n      - R3.3:\n          text: Must print an error message to stderr when an invalid option is given and exit 125.\n\n  R4:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (genv) via pkg/testutils.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: no-argument environment dump, NAME=VALUE setting, -u unsetting, -i empty environment, -0 NUL-delimited output, COMMAND execution with modified env, and exit code passthrough.\"\n      - R4.3:\n          text: Tests must verify error output and exit code for invalid options and missing commands.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/env does not implement -C (change directory) or -S (split string) GNU extensions.\n  - cmd/env does not read variable assignments from stdin; all input comes from command-line arguments.\n  - cmd/env does not perform shell expansion on COMMAND or its arguments; exec is direct.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/env with no arguments produces the same output as genv with no arguments.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/env FOO=bar env prints an environment that includes FOO=bar, matching genv.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/env -i FOO=bar env produces only FOO=bar (plus any exec-injected variables), matching genv -i.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R4.2\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/env -u HOME env omits HOME from the output, matching genv -u HOME.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.2\n      - R4.2\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"Differential test against genv passes for environment dump, -i, -u, NAME=VALUE, -0, COMMAND execution, and exit code passthrough.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.3\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"cmd/env compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n","numLines":114,"startLine":1,"totalLines":114}}}
