{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler orchestrator) assigned task #5360: implement `cmd/env` for the go-unix-utils project, covering srd039-env requirements R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, and R2.1. This requires creating two files: `cmd/env/main.go` (the env utility) and `cmd/env/env_test.go` (differential tests). The implementation must match GNU `genv` behavior byte-for-byte, verified via differential testing against the Homebrew reference binary.\n\n   Specific requirements in scope:\n   - **R1.1**: When invoked with no arguments, print every environment variable on its own line in NAME=VALUE format and exit 0.\n   - **R1.2**: When invoked with COMMAND [ARG ...], execute COMMAND with the resulting environment after all modifications.\n   - **R1.3**: If COMMAND not found, exit 127. If found but cannot be executed, exit 126.\n   - **R2.1**: `-i` or `--ignore-environment` starts COMMAND with an empty environment. Only explicitly supplied NAME=VALUE pairs appear.\n\n   Requirements NOT in scope for this task: R2.2 (-u unset), R2.3 (NAME=VALUE parsing - though needed implicitly), R3.1 (-0 null output), R3.2 (exit code passthrough - implicit in R1.2), R3.3 (invalid option handling).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementation of GNU `env` utility\n   - Differential testing pattern via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Reference binary: `genv` from Homebrew GNU coreutils\n   - `exec.LookPath` for finding commands and reference binaries\n   - `syscall.Exec` or `os/exec` for executing child commands\n   - Exit code semantics: 126 (cannot execute), 127 (not found)\n   - Environment manipulation: `os.Environ()`, empty env with `-i`\n   - NAME=VALUE argument parsing (first arg without `=` that isn't a flag starts COMMAND)\n   - Copyright header: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n   - No git commands allowed (orchestrator manages git)\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines hard limit\n   - File size limit: 500 lines\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd039-env.yaml** (READ)\n     - Full SRD for the env utility defining all requirements, goals, non-goals, and acceptance criteria\n     - Key: R1.1 (print env), R1.2 (exec command), R1.3 (exit codes 126/127), R2.1 (-i empty env)\n     - Non-goals: No -C (chdir), No -S (split string), No stdin reading, No shell expansion\n   \n   - **pkg/sys/sigpipe.go** (PROVIDED in context)\n     - Contains `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - must be called at start of main\n     ```go\n     func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n         c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n         signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n         go func() {\n             <-c\n             os.Exit(0)\n         }()\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (PROVIDED in context)\n     - `DiffTest` struct: `Name`, `Args`, `Stdin`, `Env`, `WorkDir`, `ExitCode`, `Normalize`, `ExpectedFiles`\n     - `RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)`\n     - `BuildBinary(t, \".\")` compiles the cmd/ package\n     - `buildEnv()` merges test env with LC_ALL=C default\n\n   - **cmd/env/main.go** (TO CREATE)\n     - env utility implementation covering R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1\n   \n   - **cmd/env/env_test.go** (TO CREATE)\n     - Differential tests for R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - no code has been written.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand exact requirements before implementation\n   - No code written yet; implementation planning phase only\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The massive task prompt containing the full stitch task specification for task #5360, including all project context, SRDs, source code, constitutions, constraints, and requirements for implementing cmd/env with R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1.\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/env/main.go` implementing:\n     - R1.1: No-args environment dump (NAME=VALUE per line, exit 0)\n     - R1.2: Execute COMMAND with modified environment\n     - R1.3: Exit 127 if command not found, 126 if not executable\n     - R2.1: `-i`/`--ignore-environment` for empty environment\n     - SIGPIPE handler at start of main\n     - Proper argument parsing (flags, NAME=VALUE pairs, COMMAND detection)\n   - Create `cmd/env/env_test.go` with differential tests:\n     - Use `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")`\n     - Use `exec.LookPath(\"genv\")` with `t.Skip` fallback\n     - Test cases for: no-args dump, NAME=VALUE setting, -i empty env, command execution, exit code 127/126\n   - Verify: `go build ./cmd/env/`, `go vet ./cmd/env/`, `go test ./cmd/env/ -count=1`\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the SRD file (`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd039-env.yaml`) and was about to begin implementing the two files. No code has been written yet. The implementation plan was:\n   \n   1. Write `cmd/env/main.go` with:\n      - Copyright header\n      - `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` call\n      - Flag parsing for `-i`/`--ignore-environment` (manual parsing since env has unusual arg syntax - flags must come before NAME=VALUE and COMMAND)\n      - Logic to build environment (inherit or empty based on -i)\n      - NAME=VALUE argument collection\n      - COMMAND detection (first non-flag arg without `=`)\n      - If no COMMAND: print environment, exit 0\n      - If COMMAND: use `syscall.Exec` or `os/exec` to run it with proper exit codes\n   \n   2. Write `cmd/env/env_test.go` with differential test cases\n   \n   3. Build and test\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write both `cmd/env/main.go` and `cmd/env/env_test.go` in full, then verify with `go build`, `go vet`, and `go test`. This directly continues the task from the user's prompt which states: \"Implement srd039-env R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1\" with files to create being `cmd/env/main.go` and `cmd/env/env_test.go`. The SRD has been read and the implementation can proceed.\n\n   Key implementation considerations:\n   - env has non-standard argument parsing (not cobra/flag): flags like `-i` come first, then NAME=VALUE pairs, then COMMAND starts at first arg without `=` that isn't a flag\n   - For R1.3 exit codes: need to distinguish \"not found\" (127) vs \"permission denied\" (126) using `exec.LookPath` and error types\n   - For R2.1: when `-i` is set, start with empty `[]string{}` instead of `os.Environ()`\n   - Must handle `--` to stop option processing (standard GNU convention)\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5360/d461bfc8-ec86-4b76-a705-0ddc369f10bf.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d461bfc8-ec86-4b76-a705-0ddc369f10bf","uuid":"e5791e74-3f2e-4651-9a45-b09e10d6f172","timestamp":"2026-05-20T13:55:00.781Z","isSynthetic":true}
