{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R8Sqior9J3KXE68XdFuju6","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile my findings:\n\n## Summary of go-unix-utils Project Conventions\n\nBased on my exploration of the go-unix-utils project at `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5360`, here are the key conventions you need to follow for implementing `cmd/env`:\n\n### 1. **Manual Argument Parsing Pattern (No Cobra/Flag)**\n\nThe project uses simple manual argument parsing throughout. Here are the established patterns:\n\n**From `cmd/echo/main.go`** (lines 17-38) - Simple flag cluster parsing:\n- Iterate through `os.Args[1:]`\n- Use a helper function `isFlag()` to identify flags\n- Process flag characters in a loop before processing operands\n- Stop at the first non-flag argument\n\n**From `cmd/dirname/main.go`** (lines 31-59) - Switch-based flag handling with `--`:\n- Use a `for` loop with a `switch` on the first remaining arg\n- Handle `--help`, `--version`, and options like `-z`/`--zero`\n- Support `--` to terminate flag processing\n- Use a `goto done` pattern to exit flag parsing\n\n**From `cmd/seq/main.go`** (lines 74-100) - Complex flag/value handling:\n- Check for `--` first to consume all remaining args as operands\n- Use `strings.HasPrefix()` for long-form flags\n- Use helper functions like `parseLongFlag()` and `parseShortFlags()`\n- Return parsed options and operands separately\n\n**Pattern for `env` specifically:** Since env has unusual arg syntax (NAME=VALUE mixed with options and operands), you'll likely need:\n- Parse `-i`, `-u NAME`, `-0` flags first\n- Collect NAME=VALUE pairs while they contain `=`\n- Stop at first non-flag, non-assignment argument (which is the COMMAND)\n\n### 2. **Copyright Header Format (Exact)**\n\nEvery file must use this exact format (from any of the files, e.g., `cmd/echo/main.go` lines 1-2):\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n```\n\n### 3. **Test File Structure Using testutils.RunDiffTests**\n\nComplete example from `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5360/cmd/tee/tee_test.go` (lines 4-33):\n\n```go\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"bytes\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n)\n\nfunc TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n\tgoBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n\trefBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gtee\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Skip(\"reference binary gtee not found\")\n\t}\n\ttests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n\t\t{Name: \"passthrough_no_files\", Stdin: []byte(\"hello\\nworld\\n\")},\n\t\t{Name: \"empty_stdin\", Stdin: []byte{}},\n\t\t{Name: \"large_input\", Stdin: bytes.Repeat([]byte(\"abcdefghij\\n\"), 1000)},\n\t\t{Name: \"no_trailing_newline\", Stdin: []byte(\"no newline\")},\n\t\t{Name: \"binary_data\", Stdin: allBytes()},\n\t}\n\ttestutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n}\n```\n\n**Key patterns:**\n- `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` - compiles the current package\n- `exec.LookPath(\"g<COMMAND>\")` - finds the reference binary (e.g., `genv` for env)\n- `t.Skip()` if reference binary not found\n- Build a `[]testutils.DiffTest` slice with test cases\n- Each test specifies: `Name`, `Args` (optional), `Stdin`, `WorkDir` (optional)\n- Call `testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)` to run differential tests\n\n**For capture with exit codes** (from tee_test.go, lines 433-451):\n```go\nfunc runCapture(\n\tt *testing.T, binary string, stdin []byte, args ...string,\n) (int, []byte, []byte) {\n\tt.Helper()\n\tcmd := exec.Command(binary, args...)\n\tcmd.Stdin = bytes.NewReader(stdin)\n\tvar stdout, stderr bytes.Buffer\n\tcmd.Stdout = &stdout\n\tcmd.Stderr = &stderr\n\terr := cmd.Run()\n\tif err == nil {\n\t\treturn 0, stdout.Bytes(), stderr.Bytes()\n\t}\n\tif exitErr, ok := errors.AsType[*exec.ExitError](err); ok {\n\t\treturn exitErr.ExitCode(), stdout.Bytes(), stderr.Bytes()\n\t}\n\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\treturn -1, nil, nil\n}\n```\n\n### 4. **Exit Codes 126/127 Handling**\n\n**No existing commands currently handle 126/127 in the codebase** (grep found no matches).\n\nHowever, the env specification (`srd039-env.yaml` line 27) explicitly requires:\n- **Exit 127** if COMMAND is not found\n- **Exit 126** if COMMAND is found but cannot be executed\n- **Exit 125** for invalid option\n- **Exit code passthrough** for successful COMMAND execution (R3.2)\n\nThis is unusual in the current codebase, which typically uses exit code 1 for general errors. For env, you'll need to handle `exec.LookPath()` failures and `exec.Cmd` execution errors appropriately.\n\n### 5. **No cmd/env/ Directory Exists**\n\nThe grep output confirmed there is no `cmd/env/` directory yet. The specification exists at:\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5360/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd039-env.yaml`\n\nYou will need to create the directory structure and implement it from scratch.\n\n### 6. **Standard Main Function Pattern**\n\nAll utilities follow this pattern:\n```go\nfunc main() {\n\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()  // Always called first\n\t\n\t// Parse arguments\n\targs := os.Args[1:]\n\t\n\t// Process\n\t\n\t// Exit appropriately\n\tos.Exit(exitCode)\n}\n```\n\nThe `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` is critical for proper SIGPIPE handling (especially important for utilities like `yes`, `cat`, `tee`).\n\n---\n\n**Key Files to Reference:**\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5360/cmd/echo/main.go` - Simple flag parsing\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5360/cmd/dirname/main.go` - Option/operand separation\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/c